<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Deodhai</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Deodhais</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Deodhais were one of the hereditary priestly groups of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahom-people">Ahom people</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assam">Assam</a>, alongside the Bailungs and the Mohans. They preserved the older Tai rites, language and script of the founders of the Ahom kingdom, conducted royal and ancestral ceremonies and were custodians of Ahom religious <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuscript">manuscripts</a>. Their traditions survived the gradual Hinduisation of the Ahom court from the sixteenth century onwards.</p></div>
